# Generated at boot, not source.
#
# `rustango_cms::migrations::materialize` copies the CMS baseline in here from
# the repo's own ../../migrations/ — byte-identical duplicates, ~420 KB, and
# they'd have to be re-copied on every baseline change. The framework writes
# system/migrations/ the same way. Only this example's OWN migration
# (0004_create_cms_article_page.json, emitted by `makemigrations`) is source,
# so it's un-ignored below.
#
# A real project generated by `rcms new` commits all of these — it has no
# repo to materialize from. This example does, which is why it differs.
migrations/*
!migrations/0004_create_cms_article_page.json
!migrations/0005_create_demo_sectioned_page.json
!migrations/0012_create_demo_product_feed.json
system/
var/
